course: dictionary
lesson: 7483
title: Positively and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one to use. «She answered positively.» Here positively means in a hopeful, good way: she said yes, or said something encouraging. The words around it are the clue.
explain: Now look at «It was positively freezing.» Positively does not mean hopeful here. It means really or completely, and it makes freezing stronger. Check by swapping in really: «It was really freezing» still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: In science and maths, positively has a different job. «A positively charged particle» has a plus charge, and a positive number is above zero. The subject tells you which meaning to use, so read the topic as well as the sentence.
fact: Positively is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done or how strong something is.
fact: «Think positively» means to expect good things and to be hopeful.
fact: «Positively» can make an adjective stronger, as in «positively delicious», which means really delicious.
fact: «Positively» can mean certainly, without any doubt, as in «I positively know he was there».
fact: In science and maths, «positively charged» means having a plus charge, and a positive number is above zero.
exercise: «It was positively freezing.» What does positively mean here? | In a hopeful, good way | With a plus charge | Above zero | *Really, completely
exercise: «A positively charged particle» is found in which subject? | Art | Drama | *Science | Music
exercise: Which sentence uses positively to mean certainly, without any doubt? | «A positive number is above zero.» | *«I positively know he was there.» | «It was positively freezing.» | «She answered positively.»
test: Your teacher says, «Think positively about your test.» What does positively suggest? | With a plus charge | *In a hopeful, good way | Without any doubt | Really, completely
test: In maths, what does positive mean? | Never counted | Below zero | *Above zero | Equal to zero
exam: In «Jesus put it positively in Matthew 7:12», what does positively suggest? | Without any reason | With a plus charge | *In a good, helpful way that asks us to do good | Very loudly
